# Frontend Rules

- Read `docs/01-brand.md`, `docs/02-design-system.md`, `docs/04-ux-rules.md`, `docs/06-coding-rules.md`, and `docs/08-components.md` when relevant.
- Reuse existing design tokens and components before creating new ones.
- Follow the existing React/Next.js rendering patterns.
- Keep server/client boundaries intentional.
- Handle loading, empty, error, disabled, and success states where applicable.
- Preserve responsive behavior and accessibility.
- Do not introduce arbitrary colors, spacing, typography, or interaction patterns when a design token exists.
- Validate affected UI with the repository's configured checks and tests.
